    {
      "id": "9a63afdcc638a10b2f94fa5a72c467e19795dffa",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1631969851,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I'm not seeing why this particular meta data from a specific file format needs to be present in the status bar. IMHO, this needs to be as clean as possible.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2398962,
            "username": "JaapKeuter",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Jaap Keuter",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/722b0c520542a23cb8f8ea7070a45c88f9e9214dc700ac151e419e9649e0304e?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/JaapKeuter"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-11-02T15:28:56.011Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-11-02T15:28:56.011Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 261134065,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 13010,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2a5d9ebdd2246fad6c606c19093c74339a4c47fe",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1632333066,
          "type": null,
          "body": "There's some discussion in the original bug, but I think it's because\n\nSecrets aren't saved when converting formats (we should probably warn about that, there's another bug).\nFor security reasons, it's good to be reminded that there are secrets present in the file, without having to remember to open the dialog.\n\nPossibly not a great argument, but I think it's more useful than comments (which is similar) or some of the other status bar information (some of which is optional.) Having a count of packets, comments, and decryption secrets seems reasonable to me, though I would probably lean against putting the name resolution information in the status bar as suggested in the one bug, it doesn't seem quite as important. (And because I wouldn't include the NRB, I do see your argument here, it is reasonable.)\n\nTheoretically if any other file format starts supporting embedded secrets, like with comments wiretap should be made to support reading them and converting them internally into a DSB. It's just that none of them do (though I think it's one of the more powerful arguments for pcapng.)\n\nI could split off the status bar from the Capture File Properties dialog part if that makes it easier to get consensus.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-11-02T20:11:04.232Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-11-02T20:13:47.526Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 261134065,
